# Astrape AI — Frontend Design System

## Design Language: "Spectral" Glassmorphism

Astrape uses a **dark-first, translucent aesthetic** — layered depth, continuous gradient meshes, surgical accent colors. Every screen should feel like a data terminal floating in deep space. Never produce generic, flat, or "light-mode-ported-dark" UI.

### Core Principles

- **Elevation via opacity** — higher cards use higher background opacity. Never use blur except on modal overlays (performance constraint on 60 Hz mobile panels).
- **Surgical illumination** — accent glows are applied to at most ONE primary element per screen. Overuse destroys hierarchy.
- **Data density with breathing room** — pack metrics tightly but always preserve clear visual rhythm through consistent spacing.
- **Mono for data, Grotesk for prose** — all numeric/metric values use `font-mono`; labels, headings, and body copy use `font-sans` (Space Grotesk).

---

## Design Tokens

### Colors (CSS Variables → Tailwind)

```css
/* Base backgrounds — layered depth */
--bg0: #08080F   → bg-bg0         /* deepest layer, page background */
--bg1: #0F0F1A   → bg-bg1         /* section backgrounds */
--bg2: #141424   → bg-bg2         /* card backgrounds */
--bg3: #1C1C30   → bg-bg3         /* elevated cards, code blocks */

/* Glassmorphism surfaces */
--glass:  rgba(255,255,255,0.04)  → bg-glass
--glass2: rgba(255,255,255,0.08)  → bg-glass2
--border: rgba(255,255,255,0.07)  → border-border

/* Accent palette — use sparingly */
--blue:  #4621FF  → text-blue  / bg-blue  / border-blue   /* primary CTA, active states */
--teal:  #00C8A8  → text-teal  / bg-teal  / border-teal   /* success, HRV, recovery */
--amber: #FFCB88  → text-amber / bg-amber / border-amber  /* warnings, TSB, effort */
--red:   #F07178  → text-red   / bg-red   / border-red    /* alerts, max HR, danger */

/* Semantic accent dims (15% opacity backgrounds) */
--blue-dim:  rgba(70,33,255,0.15)   → bg-blue-dim
--teal-dim:  rgba(0,200,168,0.15)   → bg-teal-dim
--amber-dim: rgba(255,203,136,0.15) → bg-amber-dim
--red-dim:   rgba(240,113,120,0.15) → bg-red-dim

/* Text hierarchy */
--text0: #F0F0FF                    → text-text0   /* primary text */
--text1: rgba(240,240,255,0.65)     → text-text1   /* secondary text */
--text2: rgba(240,240,255,0.35)     → text-text2   /* labels, placeholders */
```

### Typography

```
Display / Headings  → font-sans    (Space Grotesk, loaded via Google Fonts)
Labels / Data / Code → font-mono  (Space Mono, loaded via Google Fonts)
```

**Rules:**
- All numeric metric values → `font-mono` (scores, HR, watts, paces, counts)
- Section labels and uppercase tags → `font-mono text-[10px] tracking-widest uppercase`
- Body copy and descriptions → `font-sans`
- Never use Inter, Roboto, or system-ui as a primary font

