## Svelte 5 Patterns

Always use **Svelte 5 runes**. Never use the legacy `$:`, `writable()`, or `export let` reactive patterns.

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  // Props
  let { value = 0, label = '' }: { value: number; label: string } = $props();

  // Local state
  let loading = $state(false);
  let items = $state<string[]>([]);

  // Derived values
  let displayValue = $derived(value > 0 ? value.toFixed(1) : '—');

  // Side effects
  $effect(() => {
    // runs reactively; clean up with returned function
    return () => {};
  });
</script>
```

### Event handling

Use `onclick`, `oninput`, `onkeydown` (lowercase, no `on:` prefix — Svelte 5 syntax).

```svelte
<button onclick={() => handleClick()}>Click</button>
<input oninput={(e) => (value = e.currentTarget.value)} />
```

### Stores (rune-based)

```ts
// lib/stores/example.svelte.ts
function createStore() {
  let _value = $state(0);
  return {
    get value() { return _value; },
    set(v: number) { _value = v; }
  };
}
export const exampleStore = createStore();
```

